en:
Good, I'm glad.
Then I'll talk.
First, let me ask all of you something.{p}

Actually, I'm the type who sees spirits pretty easily.
So Hino was always asking me about it.
He wanted an article out of it, so he really wanted me to do a report on the forbidden restroom.{p}

I took a plunger out of the cleaning closet.
Then I probed deep down into the toilet.
Out came a commuter pass case.{p}

There was a photo of a girl inside it.
"Hosoda...!"
A voice came from behind me.{p}

The rapping echoed loudly even out there.
And I could hear something like sobbing, too.
I got away from there for the time being.{p}

Maybe what had kept him tied to the forbidden restroom was that photo of the girl.
Maybe since the photo had come out of the toilet, he didn't need to stay there anymore.
If that was it, there was no point searching other restrooms, right?{p}

...He wasn't anywhere.
I was worn out from searching and thought I'd just go home.
So I decided to take one more look at the forbidden restroom before I left.{p}

...His name was Yoshinori Inoue.
He said he'd been walking home from school with his little sister when a hit-and-run driver struck them.
And his sister died.{p}

Of course, it was the driver who did the hit-and-run.
But he couldn't forgive the student who'd been riding in that car for going to school like nothing had happened.
He said he'd been angry enough to want to kill him.{p}

That's right, the forbidden restroom.
He threw up in one of the stalls.
But no matter how much he threw up, the agony wouldn't stop.{p}

The hit-and-run driver was his father.
I'd just assumed his family was rich.
I'd thought the one driving him to and from school was a private chauffeur.{p}

"Thank you..."
Had I really done something worth being thanked for?
I didn't know, but I couldn't just leave the body lying there, right?{p}

...I see.
Well, I've got a really strong sixth sense, you know.
I can make friends with ordinary people and with ghosts.{p}

I should examine the toilet more closely.
To do that, just looking at it wouldn't cut it.
That's what I thought.{p}

"Come on, Hosoda. Let's go home."
"But, Hino..."
"Never mind that, we're going."{p}

Whenever I try to go into the forbidden restroom, the door absolutely won't open.
I can't get in.
I had no choice but to give up the investigation...{p}

...Huh? Is there more to it, you ask?
Who knows... My story's over.
Whose turn is it next?{p}

I can't forgive anyone who'd do something that horrible to my friend.
He deserves to die.
I decided to grant my friend's wish.{p}

I gently laid my hand over the spot where his hand was, and made him a promise.
"I'll do as you say."
The next day, I called that student to the forbidden restroom.{p}
